T*
(Topic: Python Function Parameters and Mutable Defaults) Tj T*
T*
(1. Function parameter defaults are evaluated once at definition time.) Tj T*
(2. When a default parameter is assigned a mutable container like [] or {},) Tj T*
(   subsequent calls share the identical memory reference.) Tj T*
(3. To avoid unexpected state retention across calls, use None as default:) Tj T*
(   def safe_append\(item, target=None\):) Tj T*
(       if target is None:) Tj T*
(           target = []) Tj T*
(       target.append\(item\)) Tj T*
(       return target) Tj T*
T*
(4. Python binds default arguments to the function object attribute __defaults__.) Tj T*
(5. Modifying default arguments in place is one of the most common student bugs.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
