T*
(Topic: Python Built-in Sequences and Index Boundaries) Tj T*
T*
(1. Sequences in Python are zero-indexed from 0 to len\(seq\) - 1.) Tj T*
(2. An IndexError is raised whenever an index outside this range is requested.) Tj T*
(3. Common off-by-one bug pattern: range\(len\(items\) + 1\).) Tj T*
(4. Best practice is to iterate directly over elements: for item in items:) Tj T*
(5. KeyError is raised when accessing a non-existent key in a dictionary.) Tj T*
(6. Always use dict.get\(key, default\) for safe retrieval with fallbacks.) Tj T*
(7. ZeroDivisionError occurs when divisor evaluates to 0 at runtime.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
